### La Jolla Difference Sets Repository
- Maintainers: Daniel M. Gordon
- Home: https://dmgordo.github.io/difference-sets/
- Upstream terms: CC-BY-4.0
- Held here: Records store the parameters, the abelian group's invariant factors, and the quoted status entry. No difference sets are copied from the dataset.
- Requested citation: The dataset ships a CITATION.cff asking that it be cited using that file's metadata: Daniel M. Gordon, "La Jolla Difference Sets Repository", dataset, version 1.0, 2024, https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10775931. The CC-BY-4.0 licence also requires stating what was changed: only open parameter sets are kept here, and no difference sets are copied.

### Small Ramsey Numbers (dynamic survey DS1)
- Maintainers: Stanisław Radziszowski, Daniel Munro (Leaps in Bounds)
- Home: https://www.combinatorics.org/ojs/index.php/eljc/article/view/DS1
- Upstream terms: No formal licence stated; a living survey article published by the Electronic Journal of Combinatorics.
- Held here: Records store the two clique sizes, the survey's lower and upper bound, and the quoted description and bounds block from the tracker page the row cites. No colourings, critical graphs or reference lists are copied from either source.
- Requested citation: Cite S. Radziszowski, "Small Ramsey Numbers", Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, Dynamic Survey DS1, https://doi.org/10.37236/21, and credit Leaps in Bounds (D. Munro, https://leapsinbounds.org/) for the per-constant pages.

